@startuml
title RP2354 and FPGA interaction over the system lifecycle

hide footbox
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 100

control "RP2354 firmware" as MCU
database "Embedded bitstream\nin boot flash" as Image
participant "Trion configuration logic" as Config
participant "FPGA register design" as FPGA
participant "FPGA peripherals" as Periph
boundary "Dedicated FPGA pins" as Pins

group Configuration phase - hardware SPI at 8 MHz
  MCU -> Pins : OSC_EN high; CRESET_N low then high
  Image --> MCU : fpga_image bytes
  MCU -> Config : CS low; stream bitstream on SCK and SDIO
  loop Until configuration completes or 500 ms expires
    MCU -> Config : 32 trailing zero bytes / clocks
    Config -> Pins : CDONE level
    Pins --> MCU : Sample CDONE on RP2354 GPIO5
  end
  MCU -> Config : CS high
  MCU -> MCU : Deinitialize SPI0; park CS high, SCK low, SDIO input
  Config -> FPGA : Start design; internal 256-cycle reset at 32 MHz
end

group Bring-up validation - bit-banged three-wire register bus
  MCU -> MCU : Wait 1500 ms
  MCU -> FPGA : PING command 0x9F
  FPGA --> MCU : Design ID 0xB8 on shared SDIO
  MCU -> MCU : Cache FPGA ready verdict
end

group Boot PSRAM analyzer marker
  MCU -> FPGA : WRITE register 0x15 = 1
  FPGA -> Periph : Drive GPO0 / board PIN13 / ball F5 high
  MCU -> MCU : Run the intentional PSRAM POST
  MCU -> FPGA : WRITE register 0x15 = 0 when POST returns
  FPGA -> Periph : Drive GPO0 low
end

group Normal runtime control and observation
  MCU -> FPGA : Write LED RGB, brightness and enable registers
  FPGA -> Periph : Generate active-low PWM for physical RGB LED
  Periph -> FPGA : SW1 active-low input
  FPGA -> FPGA : Debounce; track level, sticky event and press count
  MCU -> FPGA : Read status, button and count registers
  FPGA --> MCU : One register byte per read transaction
  MCU -> FPGA : Write tick-capture register
  FPGA -> FPGA : Latch free-running 32-bit counter
  MCU -> FPGA : Read four tick bytes
  FPGA --> MCU : Coherent counter snapshot
end

group Once-per-second runtime health monitoring
  Pins --> MCU : CDONE and STATUS levels
  MCU -> FPGA : PING and optional LED readback
  FPGA --> MCU : ID and register values
  alt Three consecutive failures and automatic recovery enabled
    MCU -> Config : Re-run complete configuration sequence
    Config -> FPGA : Fresh design and register defaults
    MCU -> FPGA : Repaint heartbeat state after successful validation
  else Healthy or recovery disabled
    MCU -> MCU : Continue foreground loop
  end
end

note over MCU, FPGA
  The MCU is the runtime bus controller. The FPGA never initiates a
  three-wire transaction; it returns data only while the MCU clocks a read.
  CDONE and STATUS are the independent FPGA-to-MCU indications.
end note

@enduml
